- prerelease-dist-tag: The release workflow publishes any semver prerelease version (one with a hyphenated pre-release part, such as 1.0.0-rc.1) under the npm `next` dist-tag and a final version without a dist-tag override, so a release candidate never moves npm `latest`.
- docs-test-after-release: The compatibility docs check accepts the three Gate: changelog entries in whichever CHANGELOG.md section holds them, so docs checks and npm test still pass once the entries move from Unreleased to the 1.0.0-rc.1 section.
- release-channel-docs: README's project status tells users that release candidates are published under the npm `next` dist-tag while `@latest` stays on the newest final release.
